sources:
  - backend/docs/architecture
  - frontend/docs/architecture
  - backend/tools/gen-architecture.py
instructions: >
  Producer id iotsupport-app, two subprojects. The hand-authored artifacts are
  backend/docs/architecture/architecture.yaml and frontend/docs/architecture/architecture.yaml;
  edit those. backend/docs/architecture/firmware-products.yaml maps firmware codes to
  product UUIDs and is an input to the generator below.

  backend/tools/gen-architecture.py is a CI-only generator (the Generate stage of
  Jenkinsfile.architecture, job AaC/IoTSupport): it fetches the published dataset,
  reads the live ESP32 device fleet from the prd API with a client-credentials
  token, and emits a second, generated artifact of device:/ss: elements with
  deterministic uuid5 ids. It cannot run outside CI and its output is not in git;
  do not try to produce it. Change the generator only when the shape of what it
  emits must change, never to add data; add devices and firmware through the
  application, not the model.
